Scope: git-topology.py, its integration test, and the one-line README
entry, committed together. The README and the tool's docstring/usage now
describe the descendant orientation. The untracked .claude/ and CLAUDE.md
are left out.

Orientation: an earlier draft of this tool nested under the nearest
ancestor, which put the rebase target (the most-ahead tip) at the deepest
indent and the base at the flush-left root -- backwards for the
--update-refs workflow, where you rebase the tip and let --update-refs
carry the bases. Inverted to nest under the nearest descendant so pure
tips are the roots and grep -v '^ ' yields the branches to rebase. The
grep hint is kept out of --help by request; it lives in the module
docstring only.

A co-located guard was needed: when several branches share a tip OID they
are each other's ancestor-or-self, so without excluding equal-OID pairs
from the candidate-drop step they would eliminate one another and a real
base could end up parentless. The guard keeps them all as roots.

Tests pass 18/18 (python3 + git, autopep8 and shellcheck clean). The
oracle check caught a real wiring bug while developing: the script
defaults to refs/heads/ with no args, but the oracle's for-each-ref with
no pattern listed every ref, so check_roots now mirrors the refs/heads/
default.
